String manipulation means performing different operations on text, such as:
- Finding the length.
- Converting uppercase and lowercase.
- Joining two strings.
- Extracting characters.
- Checking whether a word exists.

Uppercase and lowercase
-----------------------
var name = "swift programming"
print(name.uppercased())  -->SWIFT PROGRAMMING
print(name.lowercased())  -->swift programming

Find string length
------------------
var name = "xxx"
print(name.count)----->3

Combine two strings
-------------------
var first = "deva"
var last = "nath"
var fullname = first+" "+last
print(fullname)----->devanath

String interpolation
--------------------
> String interpolation means inserting a variable inside a string using \().

var name = "deva"
var age = 21
print("My name is \(name)")   --->My name is deva
print("My age is \(age)")      --->My age is 21

Check whether a word exists
---------------------------
var message = "I love Swift programming"
if message.contains("Swift") {
    print("Word found")   ----->Word found
} else {
    print("Word not found")
}
